    "proximate_text": "The Root Cause of this event is that RBS did not challenge an assumption regarding the applicability of double isolation on the supply header of SSW. Because of these assumptions, SWP-MOV57A and SWP-MOV57B were not properly characterized by the In-Service Testing program and credit was taken for the isolation capability of check valves in-line with SWP-MOV57A and SWP-MOV57B.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "unchallenged design assumption led to inadequate IST classification of isolation valves",
    "provisional": true
