  "notes": "Cause code TBD in FORM-366 fields is copied verbatim; category 'provisional' per schema default since no official cause code was assigned in the source fields. Both MOV57A and MOV57B leakage failures modeled as parallel FailureMode nodes stemming from the same miscategorization failure, each leading to the same UHS-inoperable consequence per rule 5. No BACKED_UP_BY edges emitted since no operable backup to UHS/SSW is stated as available during the leakage window. In-line check valves are mentioned only as the (mistaken) basis for isolation credit, not as an operable backup system during the event, so no System/Component node created for them. Previous occurrence LER key recorded as stated in narrative ('LER 2014-004-00'), noting the report text shows partial number '201■004-00' due to OCR corruption; used the clearly legible portion per the instructions to copy the LER number exactly as stated."
